     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The dose is also five times the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any accepted protocol that uses 1000 mg/day of sertraline. Higher doses don't have evidence of added benefit, and they carry a real risk of serious harm.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest instead:\n- **Pharmacy review:** Ask the pharmacist to review the dose directly. They can verify it and, if needed, override it through the hospital's high-dose process.\n- **Specialist confirmation:** Get the specialist's recommendation documented as a direct order or consult note that includes the rationale and the monitoring plan, such as ECG and serotonin toxicity checks.\n- **Other options:** If standard dosing failed, the specialist may prefer augmentation, a switch to another agent, or a dose up to 200 mg/day. I can enter any of those.\n\nI can enter sertraline at a dose of 200 mg/day or lower now if you'd like. If the high dose is verified through pharmacy or your institution's override process, tell me and we can go from there."
      }
     ],
